# .gitattributes
#
# ⛔ THE STATEMENT'S PROSE SEED MUST CHECK OUT AS LF.
#
# `src/lib/content/statementProse.md` is assembled byte-for-byte with §6, which
# is generated in memory and is therefore always LF. `core.autocrlf=true` — the
# default on Windows — would hand the app a CRLF seed, the assembled document
# would carry both endings, and `npm run check:statement-render` would fail on
# every machine except the one the file was written on. That is precisely the
# class of fault this project keeps finding: works here, broken there, and
# nothing in the build can see it.
#
# ⚠ Belt and braces only. The parser normalises line endings anyway, because
# prose also arrives from a browser textarea, where the HTML specification says
# a submitted value uses CRLF. This pins the checkout so the two never disagree
# in the first place.
src/lib/content/*.md text eol=lf
